---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Noise &amp; Error Correction — Shyam Prasad Rao" description="Where noise comes from, how we model it, how we measure it, and what we do about it.">
  <div class="crumbs"><a href="/atlas">atlas</a><span class="sep">/</span>noise &amp; error correction</div>
  <h1 class="page">Noise &amp; Error Correction</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="margin-top:10px;font-size:17px">Read left to right: where noise comes from, how we model it, how we write it down, how we measure it, and what we do about it. Characterization is the bridge almost nobody draws.</p>

  <div class="legend">
    <span><span class="dotk done"></span>published</span>
    <span><span class="dotk wip"></span>drafting</span>
    <span><span class="dotk soon"></span>coming soon</span>
  </div>

  <div class="plate">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 960 330" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Noise and error correction concept map">
      <defs>
        <marker id="arr2" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 1 L 9 5 L 0 9" fill="none" stroke="#A9A395" stroke-width="1.3"/>
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- chain edges -->
      <path class="edge2" d="M 185 135 L 218 110" marker-end="url(#arr2)"/>
      <path class="edge2" d="M 388 105 L 420 135" marker-end="url(#arr2)"/>
      <path class="edge2" d="M 578 150 L 610 115" marker-end="url(#arr2)"/>
      <path class="edge2" d="M 780 110 L 812 135" marker-end="url(#arr2)"/>

      <!-- feedback edge -->
      <path class="edge2 lead" d="M 880 265 C 800 320, 300 320, 115 240" marker-end="url(#arr2)"/>
      <rect class="elabel-bg" x="420" y="297" width="150" height="13"/><text class="elabel" x="495" y="307" text-anchor="middle">changes the noise you see</text>

      <!-- 1 Sources -->
      <g>
        <rect class="b wip" x="25" y="135" width="160" height="105"/>
        <text class="btitle" x="37" y="155">1 &middot; Sources</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="37" y="173">&middot; Environment</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="37" y="187">&middot; Crosstalk</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="37" y="201">&middot; Control Errors &#9702;</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="37" y="215">&middot; Measurement Errors &#9702;</text>
      </g>
      <!-- 2 Models -->
      <g>
        <rect class="b done" x="218" y="30" width="170" height="105"/>
        <text class="btitle" x="230" y="50">2 &middot; Models</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="230" y="68">&middot; Bit Flip &middot; Phase Flip</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="230" y="82">&middot; Depolarizing</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="230" y="96">&middot; Amplitude Damping</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="230" y="110">&middot; Dephasing &#9702;</text>
      </g>
      <!-- 3 Representation -->
      <g>
        <rect class="b done" x="420" y="135" width="158" height="105"/>
        <text class="btitle" x="432" y="155">3 &middot; Representation</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="432" y="173">&middot; Density Matrix</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="432" y="187">&middot; Kraus Operators</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="432" y="201">&middot; Superoperators</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="432" y="215">&middot; Choi Matrix</text>
      </g>
      <!-- 4 Characterization -->
      <g>
        <rect class="b wip" x="610" y="15" width="170" height="119"/>
        <text class="btitle" x="622" y="35">4 &middot; Characterization</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="622" y="53">&middot; State &middot; Process Tomography</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="622" y="67">&middot; Randomized Benchmarking</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="622" y="81">&middot; Cycle Benchmarking &#9702;</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="622" y="95">&middot; Gate Set Tomography &#9676;</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="622" y="109">&middot; Mirror RB &#9676;</text>
      </g>
      <!-- 5 Mitigation -->
      <g>
        <rect class="b done" x="812" y="135" width="140" height="133"/>
        <text class="btitle" x="824" y="155">5 &middot; Mitigation</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="824" y="173">&middot; Error Mitigation</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="824" y="187">&middot; Twirling</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="824" y="201">&middot; Surface Code</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="824" y="215">&middot; Decoders &#128679;</text>
        <text class="bitem" x="824" y="229">&middot; Fault Tolerance &#9676;</text>
      </g>

      <rect class="elabel-bg" x="158" y="106" width="72" height="13"/><text class="elabel" x="194" y="116" text-anchor="middle">give rise to</text>
      <rect class="elabel-bg" x="356" y="112" width="84" height="13"/><text class="elabel" x="398" y="122" text-anchor="middle">formalized as</text>
      <rect class="elabel-bg" x="548" y="122" width="80" height="13"/><text class="elabel" x="588" y="132" text-anchor="middle">estimated via</text>
      <rect class="elabel-bg" x="756" y="112" width="48" height="13"/><text class="elabel" x="780" y="122" text-anchor="middle">informs</text>

      <g class="maplegend">
        <text x="25" y="285">&#9702; drafting&#160;&#160;&#160;&#9676; coming soon</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <div class="plate-caption">fig. 2 &mdash; read left to right; the dotted return arrow is the loop most textbooks omit.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lately" style="margin-top:36px"><b>Why I drew it this way:</b> textbooks teach models and codes in separate chapters, so learners never see that characterization is the bridge &mdash; you can't correct what you can't measure. Column 4 is where I've spent the last six months.</div>
</Base>
